 
<section class="mx-6 my-8 p-5">
    <div class="flex flex-col justify-center items-center">
        <p class="text-4xl font-semibold ">FAQ</p>
        <p class="text-xl w-200 text-center my-2 text-primary-content-para">
            You Can Explore Frequently asked Questions from Here . Maybe you can find an answer to your question!
        </p>
    </div>
    <div class=" flex flex-col justify-center items-center gap-4  my-12">
        <details class="w-250 collapse collapse-arrow bg-base-100 border border-neutral bg-base-200" name="my-accordion-det-1">
            <summary class="collapse-title font-semibold text-xl">What is StuMap? </summary>
            <div class="collapse-content text-xl mx-4 text-primary-content-para">
                StuMap is a roadmap-based learning platform where students can follow structured paths, access curated materials, and track their progress.

            </div>
        </details>
        <details class="w-250 collapse collapse-arrow bg-base-100 border border-neutral bg-base-200" name="my-accordion-det-1">
            <summary class="collapse-title font-semibold text-xl">Who can use StuMap?  </summary>
            <div class="collapse-content text-xl mx-4 text-primary-content-para">
                There is two types of users:
                <ul class="list-disc px-8">
                    <li>Students who can explore and enroll in roadmaps and courses</li>
                    <li>Contributors who create courses and roadmaps for students</li>
            </ul>
                </div>
        </details>
        <details class="w-250 collapse collapse-arrow bg-base-100 border border-neutral bg-base-200" name="my-accordion-det-1">
            <summary class="collapse-title font-semibold text-xl">How do I enroll in a course or roadmap?   </summary>
            <div class="collapse-content text-xl mx-4 text-primary-content-para">
                You have to login First, Then You can enroll directly from the course or roadmap page. Your enrollment will be tracked in your dashboard.

            </div>
        </details>
        <details class="w-250 collapse collapse-arrow bg-base-100 border border-neutral bg-base-200" name="my-accordion-det-1">
            <summary class="collapse-title font-semibold text-xl">How do I become a contributor?  </summary>
            <div class="collapse-content text-xl mx-4 text-primary-content-para">
                Submit a contributor request by creating an account as a contributor with your specialization and certificate. Admins will review and approve or reject your request.
            </div>
        </details>
        <details class="w-250 collapse collapse-arrow bg-base-100 border border-neutral bg-base-200" name="my-accordion-det-1">
            <summary class="collapse-title font-semibold text-xl">What kind of content can I upload as a contributor?  </summary>
            <div class="collapse-content text-xl mx-4 text-primary-content-para">
                You can upload materials such as articles, videos, books, tutorials, exams, and more. Each material must be linked to a course.
            </div>
        </details>
        <details class="w-250 collapse collapse-arrow bg-base-100 border border-neutral bg-base-200" name="my-accordion-det-1">
            <summary class="collapse-title font-semibold text-xl">When I upload a course as a contributor,Does my courses need approval?  </summary>
            <div class="collapse-content text-xl mx-4 text-primary-content-para">
                Yes, all courses and materials require admin approval before they are visible to students.
            </div>
        </details>
        <details class="w-250 collapse collapse-arrow bg-base-100 border border-neutral bg-base-200" name="my-accordion-det-1">
            <summary class="collapse-title font-semibold text-xl">How do certificates work?  </summary>
            <div class="collapse-content text-xl mx-4 text-primary-content-para">
                Contributors can upload certificates to validate their expertise. Admins must approve certificates before they appear on the site.
            </div>
        </details>

    </div>
    </section>